---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { NAV, SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description="Itemized's mission to reduce household food waste, how its single-binary Go and SQLite architecture stays simple, and how to follow or contribute on GitHub."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>Practical home inventory, on a mission to reduce food waste.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Itemized was built to help households waste less food by making tracking your pantry, fridge, freezers, and storage shelves fast enough that everyone actually uses it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Our mission</h2>
      <p>
        Our mission is to reduce household food waste. Most wasted food is not neglected on purpose; it is simply forgotten behind newer groceries, buried in a chest freezer, or bought in duplicate because nobody knew what was already at home. Itemized makes it effortless to scan purchases, see where every item is stored, and surface what is set to expire so food gets eaten before it spoils.
      </p>

      <h2>Design principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Fast on real devices:</strong> Whether you are checking your shopping list at the grocery store on your phone or scanning a delivery with a USB barcode scanner at home, common actions take seconds.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Simple to operate:</strong> Itemized ships as a single Go binary with an embedded React SPA and a single SQLite database in WAL mode. There is no separate database server, cache, or print daemon to babysit.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Built for households, not enterprises:</strong> Nested locations, expiration rules for opening and freezing, universal label printing with a visual label designer, native Web Push daily digests, and simple Admin/Member roles cover real home workflows cleanly.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Yours to keep:</strong> No subscriptions, no mandatory cloud account, and plain SQLite storage you can back up anywhere.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Open source on GitHub</h2>
      <p>
        Itemized is open source (AGPL-3.0) and developed in the open at <a href={SITE.appRepo}>github.com/itemizedapp/itemized</a>. Bug reports and feature ideas are welcome via GitHub Issues; external pull requests are not accepted.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={SITE.appRepo}>
          <Icon name="star" size={16} />
          <span>View on GitHub</span>
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={SITE.issues}>Report an Issue</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={SITE.demo}>Try Live Demo</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={NAV.selfHost}>Self-Host Guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
